    structure: "A gate is a named point in the lifecycle (pre training checkpoint, pre deployment, before a new tool or permission) with a written battery of evaluations and pass criteria agreed before the run. The battery has three parts: capability evaluations that detect whether the model crossed a threshold of concern, safety evaluations that measure refusal and harmful output under adversarial prompting, and security evaluations that test the deployed system for injection, exfiltration and excessive agency. Results are produced by a team that does not report to the team that wants to ship, recorded with the exact model version and settings, and compared against criteria. A fail blocks the stage until mitigations are added and the battery is rerun. Evaluations are themselves versioned, and a schedule triggers reruns when effective compute or fine tuning progress exceeds a stated increment.",
