    structure: "Every dataset entering training has a manifest: source URLs or providers, collection timestamps, licence terms, the hash of the raw snapshot, and each transformation applied (filtering, deduplication, labelling) with the code version that applied it. Manifests are signed and stored with the dataset. A training run records the manifests it consumed, so any model version can be traced back to exact data. Before training, a gate checks manifests for missing licences, sources on a blocklist, and snapshot hashes that differ from the pinned ones. Content from the open web is snapshotted and hashed at collection so later changes to the source (including domain takeover) cannot alter what trains. Sampled audits compare dataset contents against manifests, and poisoning detectors run over high influence data slices.",
